      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "eadb94b71a37ca49cda870544d49fe8893d616b4",
            "subject": "LU-16489 tests: lustre-rsync-test/2c sync last unlinks"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-08-11 18:03:36.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-08-11 19:56:34.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20580 o2iblnd: don't sleep in atomic in kiblnd_startup()",
        "message": "LU-20580 o2iblnd: don't sleep in atomic in kiblnd_startup()\n\nkiblnd_startup() queried the net device from inside the\nwrite_lock_irqsave(&kiblnd_data.kib_global_lock) section.\nlnet_get_link_status() takes rtnl_lock(), which is a mutex and\ncan sleep, so the query ran with preemption disabled and\ninterrupts off.\n\nWhile rtnl_mutex is free the mutex fast path does not schedule\nand nothing is reported. When another task holds rtnl_mutex,\n__mutex_lock_slowpath() calls schedule_preempt_disabled() and\nthe kernel reports \"BUG: scheduling while atomic\". This is\nreached at boot, when the network subsystem holds rtnl_mutex\nwhile LNet is configured, and the node does not boot.\n\nschedule_debug() then calls preempt_count_set(PREEMPT_DISABLED),\nwhich leaves the count unbalanced.\n\nSample the interface state before the lock is taken, and take\nkib_global_lock only to link the net and record the result.\nkiblnd_set_ni_fatal_on() walks ibd_nets, so it stays inside the\nlock and after the list_add_tail().\n\nThe query was already inside the lock before the Fixes commit,\nbut did not sleep until that commit added rtnl_lock() to\nlnet_get_link_status(). The RCU read section that once wrapped\nthe query was removed later, which left the sleep in place.\n\nFixes: aebedbe75007 (\"LU-19707 lnet: fix RTNL assert in LNet on v6.15\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I19b49b26417da5c66be52f085a875a84b5feb6ed\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
